  "description": "The proposed refurbishment of Varcoe Gardens Batford Playspace will transform an underused and fragmented area of open space into a welcoming, inclusive, and multifunctional environment for residents of all ages. The proposals entail combining the two currently segregated areas into a single, cohesive and legible space that supports a wider range of activities.\n\nThe scheme includes reprofiling the site to improve usability, accessibility, and spatial coherence, alongside the introduction of new play, fitness and recreational features. A fenced play area is proposed above the existing attenuation tank, providing a dedicated space for informal sports while making efficient use of the site’s constraints. Overall, the development will deliver a high-quality landscape that enhances play provision, encourages social interaction, and supports community health and wellbeing.\n",
